  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In 260, the Persian king Shapur captured the emperor Valerian. No Roman emperor had ever been taken prisoner.",
   "say": "In two sixty, the Persian king Shapur captured the emperor Valerian. No Roman emperor had ever been taken prisoner."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Roman writers claimed Shapur used him as a footstool to climb onto his horse. Valerian died a captive."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What happened to the empire?",
   "scene": "split",
   "date": ""
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "It broke into three. In the west, Gaul and Britain went their own way. In the east, Queen Zenobia of Palmyra took Syria and Egypt."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Who put it back together?",
   "scene": "zenobia",
   "move": {
