  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Aurelian, a tough soldier emperor. In four years he defeated Zenobia and the Gallic Empire, and called himself Restorer of the World."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "He also gave Rome those walls. Then, in 275, his own officers murdered him.",
   "say": "He also gave Rome those walls. Then, in two seventy-five, his own officers murdered him."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So when did it end?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "AD 284"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "In 284, when Diocletian took power. Rome survived, but Dacia, north of the Danube, was gone for good.",
   "say": "In two eighty-four, when Diocletian took power. Rome survived, but Dacia, north of the Danube, was gone for good."
